# vdbfromlayer

- Label: VDB from Layer
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 3
- Parameters: 1 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/vdbfromlayer.html
- Summary (EN): Sets the values of an existing VDB from the closest matching values in a layer. Each VDB location is mapped onto the layer through the layer's camera projection, so the output keeps the reference VDB structure. Output: sample.
- Résumé (FR) : Remplit les valeurs d'un VDB existant à partir d'une couche, en projetant chaque voxel avec la caméra de la couche tout en gardant la structure du VDB de référence.

- Inputs meaning: ["vdb_ref: float or vector VDB serving as the activation topology for the sampled output", "layer: the layer to sample values from", "pos (optional): vector VDB whose values replace the voxels' world positions"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: the layer type the source accepts (the only parameter the page lists)"]

- Caveats: ["The page does not describe parameters beyond Signature", "Edge behaviour is not described, such as voxels that project outside the layer's camera view"]

